  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1159 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nMostly clear skies and dry conditions are expected through tomorrow. \nWinds will be from the south southeast today then becoming light and \nvariable tonight into Tuesday. A cold front is then expected to move \nthrough the area Tuesday night into Wednesday shifting winds to the \nnorth with an increase in speed. No precipitation is expected with \nthis frontal passage. The remainder of the forecast remains dry as \nridging builds west of our area late week, then over the Plains this \nweekend. As for temperatures, highs will reach into the upper 60s to \nlow 70s today and tomorrow, 60s Wednesday, then mid 50s to low 60s \nThursday and Friday. We then rebound into the 60s this weekend. Lows \nwill generally be in the 30s and low 40s with the coldest morning \nbehind Friday.",
